\newlabel{tab:base}{{2}{10}{Base cases: conditions (top) and computed electrode quantities (bottom). The sheath edge \(x_{\rm s}\) is the distance from the electrode at which \(|n_i-n_e|/n_i\) falls to \(1\,\%\), and \(\phi _{\rm s}\) is the potential there; \(\phi (L)\) is the potential at the bulk-plasma boundary. Both potentials are relative to the electrode. Fluxes are towards the electrode}{table.2}{}}
