\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Electrode quantities against the bulk temperature \(T_{\rm  bulk}\), for the cathode at \(J_{\rm  app}=1.2\times 10^{8}\ \mathrm  {A\,m^{-2}}\) (left) and the anode at \(|J_{\rm  app}|=9\times 10^{6}\ \mathrm  {A\,m^{-2}}\) (right). Filled symbols: the base cases. (a), (b) Heat flux into the electrode \(q_w\), equation~(\ref {eq:bc-qwall}). (c), (d) Ion fraction of the current density at the surface, positive for ions flowing into the cathode; at the anode the ions also flow into the surface, against the current. (e), (f) Potential at the sheath edge \(\phi _{\rm  s}\) and at the bulk-plasma boundary \(\phi (L)\), relative to the electrode. (g), (h) Sheath width \(x_{\rm  s}\), the distance from the surface at which \(|n_i-n_e|/n_i\) falls to 1\,\%.}}{17}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
